-- Arcane Mage rework (docs/arcane-mage-rework-design.md) - Rows 7-10, Phase 2 (data-only talents).
-- .claude/skills/class-rework/SKILL.md batch-and-checkpoint cadence, 4th and final Phase 2 batch.
--
-- Talents shipped this batch (6 slots):
--   (7,1) Arcane Flows      - talent 1843 (spells 44378/44379): Evocation CD retuned -1/-2min ->
--                             design's -15/-30s; Arcane Overload's new identity classmask added to
--                             the existing CD% effect's scope. Arcane Orb/Alter Time omitted - not
--                             present in this WotLK 3.3.5a ruleset (Cata-era spells). Capstone
--                             deferred.
--   (7,2) Mind Mastery      - talent 1728 (spells 31584-31586, trimmed from 5 ranks): INT% spell
--                             power already matched design as pulled (3/6/9%). Added mana cost -2/
--                             -4/-6% (all magic schools) and Brilliance Aura duration +2/+4/+6s
--                             (new classmask-scoped SpellMod, see Brilliance Aura's new identity
--                             bit below).
--   (8,0) Prismatic Cloak   - talent 1726 (spells 31574/31575, trimmed from 3 ranks): repointed to
--                             this slot in the Rows 4-6 batch (position-only then); retuned in place
--                             this batch to design's 1/2% dmg reduction + 1.5/3s Invisibility fade
--                             reduction (was 2/4/6% + 1/2/3s, 3 ranks).
--   (8,1) Temporal          - talent 1729 (was "Slow", baseline since Phase 1) repointed onto new
--        Convergence          shell spell 200078. Shell only (icon/cost/45s CD) - stack-consume +
--                             variable CD reduction logic is Phase 3.
--   (9,1) Netherwind        - talent 1846 (spells 44400/44402/44403): retuned 2/4/6% -> design's
--        Presence             1/2/3% haste. Real stock row was a flat always-on passive with zero
--                             proc/duration/stack scaffolding - the actual stacking-proc-on-cast
--                             mechanism (including cross-family Moonfire/Starfire/Starsurge
--                             triggers) is deferred whole to Phase 3, not just its capstone.
--   (10,1) Arcane Overload  - talent 1847 (was a redundant Arcane Barrage capstone grant) repointed
--                             onto new shell spell 200079 - already sitting at (10,1) exactly, no
--                             position move needed. Shell only (icon/cost/60s CD) - mana-spend AoE
--                             damage, %-max-mana regen tick and +10% spell damage buff are all one
--                             coherent Phase 3 implementation.
--
-- Also: mage.csv spell 200067 (Brilliance Aura, Phase 1) gets its first-ever classmask identity bit
-- (SpellClassMask_3 = 1) so Mind Mastery can target it with a classmask-scoped SpellMod - the first
-- talent in this rework to need to address one of Phase 1's own custom spells specifically. Two more
-- fresh identity bits minted in the same previously-untouched dword3 slot: Arcane Overload (dword3=2,
-- referenced by Arcane Flows) and Temporal Convergence (dword3=4, unused so far, reserved for future
-- rows/Phase 3 if something needs to target it).
--
-- This is the last Phase 2 data-only batch - all 10 rows / 30 talent slots of the new Arcane tree
-- are now shipped. Remaining work is entirely Phase 3 (C++) for the deferred-clause list in
-- docs/arcane-mage-rework-design.md, then Phase 4 (playtest guide).
--
-- generate.py clean (zero lint WARNINGs). test_sql_dump.py + manual balanced-statement scan clean -
-- codestyle-sql.py itself can't run in this sandbox (git fetch origin master has no network access
-- here), same accepted limitation as every prior batch.

